[gd_scene load_steps=12 format=3]

; The standard three-point HEADSTOCK — the A-frame every mounted implement bolts to, and the
; only part of an implement whose dimensions are not free: the two lower pins must meet the
; tractor's lower-link ball ends and the top pin must sit exactly at
; ImplementBase.mast_offset() = (z -0.06, y 0.533), which is what HitchLinkage closes its
; four-bar on. It lives in ONE scene so the four implements cannot drift apart from the
; linkage one at a time.
;
; Origin is ON THE LOWER PIN LINE, which is where ThreePointHitch's Mount sits, so an
; implement instancing this at its own origin is correctly hung by construction. Painted
; structural grey rather than any machine colour — it is the interface, not the machine.
; NO CollisionShape: implements are visual (ImplementBase).

